# Godot should not auto-import or compile-check anything under
# locales/. The directory holds two distinct artefacts:
#
#   * source_strings.csv — a three-column CSV
#     (id, source, context) used by `tools/validate_locale.sh`
#     to author the M1 English text. Godot's CSV translation
#     importer does not understand the third column, so
#     auto-importing the file produces a wall of "expected
#     2 locale(s)" errors.
#
#   * en.po, de.po — generated from the CSV. The PO files
#     are the canonical translation source; a separate
#     `tools/import_translations.sh` (lands with M5) is the
#     single, deterministic import path. Until that exists,
#     leaving them un-imported is the conservative choice.
#
# Translators and the validate_locale.sh script are
# filesystem-only; they do not need Godot's import pipeline
# to function. If/when we wire PO → .translation, the
# generator will write the binary .translation files into
# a subdirectory (e.g. locales/compiled/) that Godot does
# auto-import; this .gdignore stays for the source files.
